paths: file:v2/runtime/std/ui-plugin/src/main/scala/ssc/plugin/ui/UiNativePlugin.scala file:v2/runtime/std/ui-plugin/src/test/scala/ssc/plugin/ui/UiNativePluginTest.scala file:tests/e2e/ui-select-from-gate.sh file:tests/e2e/ui-provider-gap-gate.sh file:v2/BUGS.md file:tests/BUGS.md file:scripts/smoke-ci.ssc
scope: |
  Implement `selectFromView` on the native lane as a REAL primitive — the three parts the ledger entry
  names (constructor + renderer arm + field-name registration), not a descriptor alone.

  RETARGETED AFTER MEASURING, and the measurement is the reason: the claim was opened for
  `forJsonView`, but a census of who actually calls these primitives found `selectFromView` has THREE
  callers and `forJsonView` one. Measured where each stops on the native lane: `smoke-test.ssc` and
  `select-reactive-demo.ssc` both refuse on `selectFromView`; `tkv2-select-reactive` already runs.
  `forJsonView` additionally needs a JSON parser that does not exist natively (the v2 parser is
  self-hosted in std/json-core.ssc), and its own JVM reference renders EMPTY — which on a lane that
  renders server-side HTML would be a silently wrong page, not a fallback.

  Widening `paths` by one file: `tests/e2e/ui-provider-gap-gate.sh` holds a `selectFromView-refuses`
  row that MUST dissolve now that the refusal it guards is replaced by an implementation. Its other
  rows stay: the remaining four primitives still refuse, and the `still-runs-*` rows still guard the
  latent gap.
next: gate the reactive select, dissolve the stale refusal row, close the entry
